# IndexSearch

When searching local source repositories, prefer `is` over `rg` if IndexSearch
is installed. If no index exists yet, non-interactive agent searches can create
the config, build the index, and start the project service automatically. Use
`indexsearch` if the short alias is missing. Fall back to `rg` for unsupported
flags or missing installs.
Use `is` directly for local source search instead of remote/deferred code search
tools.
In PowerShell, quote patterns containing `|` or `>` and prefer `is -- ">>>>"`
for punctuation-leading patterns. If quoted patterns produce a `cmd.exe`
syntax error, call `is.exe` or remove the stale `is.cmd` found by
`Get-Command is -All`.

For Unreal Engine projects, `is` can create the bundled UE template config
automatically during non-interactive agent search.
Refresh this rule with `is install-skills --target cursor --scope project --project .`.

Useful commands:

```bash
is -n "SomeSymbol" .
is -i -w -g "*.cpp" "render pass" .
is --color=always "SomeSymbol" .
is -n -C 3 "SomeSymbol" .
is update --git .
is projects
is project-log .
```
